Yani: The cluebat.

An artifact club. Let's make it wishable, bonesable, randomly-
generatable but NOT giftable (for no reason other than to help stem
the inevitable tide of 'oh no, not another junk artifact to nerf my
altar squatting/ artiwishing' complaints).

The cluebat deals enhanced damage to all monsters, but also provides
the victim with a sudden (albeit somewhat painful) burst of mental
stimulation. The higher the enchantment, the higher the damage,
obviously, but the better the inspiration as well. The idea is to
persuade the player to hit himself repeatedly over the head with a
highly-enchanted, highly-damaging weapon in the hopes of gaining some
kind of intellectual boost. Because I'm cruel like that.

Aplying the Cluebat to the player:
**********************************

When the player is hit by the cluebat (including if he hits *himself*
with it), the effects per-whack (aside from the obvious physical
damage) are as follows:

ALL cluebat hits carry a chance of stunning and/ or confusion.
Stun only:        10% blessed bat. 20% uncursed bat. 30% cursed bat.
Confuse only:     10% blessed bat. 20% uncursed bat. 30% cursed bat.
Stun AND confuse: 5% blessed bat.  10% uncursed bat. 30%cursed bat.
In addition to the stunning/ confusion above, select one of the
effects below:

25% chance: The player gets a clue, ie hears a rumour. (95% chance
true rumour if bat positively enchanted. 95% chance false for negative
enchantment. 50/50 chance if bat at +0.)

20% chance: No further effect.

6% chance, no further effect, but a randomnly chosen YAFM. See
footnote [1]

4% chance: Temporary [2] int modification (negative bat enchantment:
int reduced by enchantment. Bat enchanted 0 to +3: +1 int. Enchanted
+4 to +7: +2 int. Enchanted > +7: +3 int. [3]) "You feel your mind
expand/ contract." (Hallu: "Woah, you feel your mind stretching out/
shrinking")

4% chance: Temporary [2] wis modification (negative bat enchantment:
wis reduced by enchantment. Enchanted 0 to +3: +1 wis. Enchanted +4 to
+7: +2 wis. Enchanted > +7: +3 wis. [3]) Messages as above.

4% chance: Temporary [2] modification to both int AND wis, enchantment
effects as above.[3] "You feel your mind expand/contract
massively!" (Hallu: "Woah, that totally blew your mind!")

4% chance: Temporary [2] telepathy granted unless already telepathic,
in which case no effect. (negatively enchanted bat: any pre-existing
intrinsic telepathy taken away.[3]) Normal telepathy messages.

4% chance: Temporary [2] clairvoyance granted unless already
clairvoyant, in which case no effect (negatively enchanted bat:
intrinsic clairvoyance taken away. [3])

4% chance: "You feel illuminated!" (Hallu: You feel switched on,
man!") Player temporarily [2] becomes a 2-radius light source. When
timeout expires: "You feel a little dimmer."

4% chance: Enlightenment effect.

4% chance: Detect traps, as per confused ?oGD.

4% chance: Effect as per 'detect monsters' spell. (bat enchanted <=
+2: unskilled detect monsters. > +2: expert detect monsters)

4% chance: Effect as per ?oID: (negative bat enchantment: One object
identification removed from the player's memory, as per amnesia
effect. 0 to +3 enchantment: as per uncursed scroll. > +3 enchantment:
as per blessed scroll.) Message as per throne-ID.

4% chance: Effect as per !oObject detection unless bat is negatively
enchanted, in which case no effect.

4% chance: Effect as per 'magic mapping' spell. (Bat enchanted 0 to
+2: unskilled spell. Enchanted > +2: expert spell. If bat is
negatively enchanted: one level map removed from player's memory
instead. )

1% chance: RNG selects a spell at random and, if the spell is
previously unknown, it is added to the player's repertoire.[4]
(negatively enchanted bat: one random spell removed from repertoire
instead)


Using the cluebat on monsters:
************************************
Sadly, monsters don't have int or wis scores, and already seem to have
sufficient knowledge of item IDs, map layouts etc, so apart from YAFM
(You hit the goblin! --more-- A light buld appears above the goblin's
head!) there's only a limited set of effects the cluebat could have on
NPCs. Here's a few ideas though, I look forward to seeing what others
rgrn can come up with.

- Stun/confusion as per player battery.
- NPC spellcasters learn new spells/ forget spells (according to bat
enchantment.)
- Eligible monsters upgrade to casters (ie gnome-> gnome wizard) or
degrade back the other way according to bat enchantment.
- There would have to be lots of fun interactions with mindflayers.
You could bat their telepathy away for a start, switch them between
regular/master MFs, reduce/ improve the effectiveness of their
attacks, modified int bonus from cluebatted MF corpses...
- YAFM using the cluebat against the oracle.


